    "done_when": "The JT-60SA sign report produced by scripts/jt60sa_sign_cohort.py, through format_sign_report in imas_ambix/data/cocos_convention.py, states its classification from its own rows. e_Bp is measured (0, psi per radian) on row 101011, not 'requires-an-external-declaration; unknown'. The other rows' declared-flux-exponent skip reasons say that row 101011 fixes e_Bp, instead of naming section 7 as the source that would. sigma_R_phi_Z is reported as declared under decision jt60sa-source-cocos, giving SELENE's output COCOS 1 from the surviving pair (1, 2). The report states its scope: this is the COCOS of SELENE's equilibrium output; the machine takes its geometric handedness from that declaration; each diagnostic's flux and current signs are confirmed per channel in the measured data. MAST's report text and scores are unchanged, pinned by the existing test. The script's --root argument also moves the psi row's G-EQDSK input, rather than reading the module-level path, with a test that a G-EQDSK under a tmp_path root is the one read. docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-sign-cohort.html is regenerated by the script. On the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set), with IMAS_ALAMBIC_MAP_PATH unset and the worktree's maps a symlink to the main checkout's maps/, run in the foreground and capture once, to a log in the run directory whose first lines give the head revision and command and whose last line is EXIT=: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/data/test_cocos_convention.py; it exits 0, the cohort script exits 0, and uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0. A landing fragment is written to the fragment path.",
